I've written two task files and the issue responses for Day 224. Nothing was committed: session_plan/ is gitignored, so git add refused it. The files exist on disk at session_plan/task_01.md, task_02.md and issue_responses.md.

Task 1 (product, Part of #1003): a separate price for Sonnet 5.5. Right now claude-sonnet-5-5 is billed at Sonnet 5's rate, with cache reads at $0.20/M. Two sources agree it should be $0.10/M: Claude Code's changelog and the models.dev catalogue. The plan:
• Check first whether yoagent 0.24.2 already ships a Sonnet 5.5 preset, and fetch the actual rates from models.dev rather than using numbers from memory.
• If the fetch fails or the two sources disagree, change only the cache-read rate.
• Add a test, plus a check that plain claude-sonnet-5 keeps its current price unchanged.

Task 2 (product, Part of #982, plus the @danstis promise):
• `yoyo risk <unknown>` prints an error but exits 0; it will exit 2 instead. The wording and the "Available" list stay the same.
• The `yoyo todo` refusal tells users to follow #679, which is closed. It will point at #1005, which tracks restoring todos on resume. This is the outstanding promise from Discussion #682, and the task ends with a short note to @danstis there.
• Update #982's status list to add a new bug the assessment found: yoyo index <path> ignores the path, indexes the current directory instead, and says it's empty when the current directory has no source files.

